__pycache__/
*.pyc
data_store/raw/*.html
data_store/raw/*.json
data_store/processed/*.nc
# generated by the pipeline: regenerate locally, do not commit
data_store/processed/
outputs/

# The polling workbook IS committed, deliberately. It costs an ~850KB binary
# diff whenever it is re-saved, which is the price of the repository being
# self-contained: the pipeline then runs in Colab or a fresh container without
# the OneDrive path, and a reset container does not lose the poll set. Consider
# Git LFS if the history gets heavy.
#
# Its derivatives stay out. A --in-place sync writes a timestamped backup and
# --append writes a .updated copy, so without these two lines every run would
# add another 900KB binary. The paste-ready CSVs are regenerable from the
# workbook plus a scrape and are pure intermediate output.
data_store/manual/*.backup-*.xlsx
data_store/manual/*.updated.xlsx
data_store/manual/new_polls_*.csv
